+### Update — 2026-09-25: 15-LED start vs buffer occupancy
+
+Captain reported about 15 LEDs lit from about LED 4 to LED 15 on Teensy
+`20731830`. `K1LED_DUMP` on the live 128-pixel DMA image contradicts that as
+firmware occupancy.
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Image | `rt1062_k1_migration_t40_ws2812_128` source `21de29b` then dirty T0H rebuild |
+| HEX SHA256 after T0H flash | `20c810354b6033bb8400c0469ef3472180ddfcfc2fd78c8262602b92c9d0e340` |
+| Header | `MODE=WS2812_BENCH PHYSICAL=128 PIN=0 OUTPUT=A_CROP_16_143` |
+| Logical | `A LIT=142 P0=000000 P79=1B01AB P80=1B01AB P159=000000` (mode 3 bloom) |
+| Wire | 114 of 128 physical pixels nonzero; first lit=7 last lit=120 |
+| Physical 4..15 | codes 0 or 1 (almost off) |
+| Peak | physical 60..64, max channel code 21 after `max_code=32` |
+| Pad | PIN=0 MUX=00000015 PAD=00000038 MASK=00000008 |
+| Timing before | PERIOD=187 ZERO_HIGH=45 ONE_HIGH=112 (300/750 ns at 150 MHz) |
+| Timing after | PERIOD=187 ZERO_HIGH=60 ONE_HIGH=120 (400/800 ns) |
+
+The 4-to-15 window in the dump is the dark bloom edge, not the lit region.
+A chain that stops around LED 16 would show exactly that window. T0H was
+widened from the OctoWS2811 300 ns minimum to WS2812B typical 400 ns.
+Optical emission remains `UNMEASURED`. If the plate still only shows 4–15,
+the remaining discriminator is DIN on pin 0 and 5 V at LED 16, not another
+renderer rewrite.
+
+### Update — 2026-09-25: RGB sparkles at CC20=0
+
+Captain: random R/G/B sparkles across the whole strip with CC20
+(`global.master_brightness`) at 0, and still in the background at CC20 up.
+
+Two live dumps with CC20 down: logical A nearly empty, **wire HEX all 384
+bytes zero**, 128 physical pixels off, frames still incrementing. Sparkles
+were therefore not renderer occupancy. They were 0-bits on the wire being
+decoded as 1s after T0H was widened to 400 ns (ZERO_HIGH_TICKS=60). That
+also explains sparkles behind a real picture when CC20 is up: every 0-bit
+in the GRB stream is on the same threshold.
+
+Reverted T0H/T1H to OctoWS2811 300/750 ns. HEX SHA256
+`81e79c70f3dec89afd08661492f6cdf034e3fb881de6d7dd8e2088b77922bed9`.
+Brightness-zero still blacks the buffer; that path was already correct.
